-- Soonr (soonr.health, Vespexx Inc.): the Soonr couples' preconception app
-- and the Surearly SMART ovulation test reader it recommends (made by
-- Sugentech / Surearly, sold on Amazon). Catalog entries only — neither is
-- an ayna brand partner. Extracted from a regenerated
-- supabase/seed/product_catalog.sql (`npm run catalog:export`); just these
-- 2 rows, safe to run standalone. Idempotent: safe to re-run.

insert into public.product_catalog (id, name, brand, category, product_type, summary, price, image, url, tags, health_functions, where_to_buy, where_to_buy_in_stock, safety, doctor_opinion, community_review, effectiveness, clinician_opinion_source, clinician_attribution, source, internal, requires_prescription, user_rating, is_active, extra)
values
  ('d-soonr', 'Soonr: Fertility App for Couples', 'Soonr', 'tracker', 'digital', 'A preconception app built for both partners. Each person logs their own health habits (exercise, meals, supplements, symptoms, and habits they’re avoiding), and both see each other’s progress; consistent logging fills a shared "Momentum Orb." It also tracks periods, discharge, ovulation test results, and basal body temperature, predicts the fertile window, and can sync Apple Watch wrist temperature through Apple Health. For hormone readings, it pairs with the separately sold Surearly SMART test reader.', 'Free; Premium $12.99/month or $9.16/month billed yearly (launch price $5.50/month billed yearly)', '/products/soonr/soonr-app.png', 'https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515', '["fertility","pregnancy","privacy"]'::jsonb, '["cycle-tracking","fertility"]'::jsonb, '["App Store","Google Play"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Not FDA-cleared. Soonr describes itself as a wellness tool, not medical advice.","materials":"N/A (app)","recalls":"N/A","allergens":"N/A","sideEffects":"N/A (software).","opinionAlerts":"Fertile-window predictions from period and symptom logs are estimates; Soonr suggests the Surearly SMART reader for actual hormone readings. The app is new (App Store release February 2026), so there’s little long-term user feedback yet."}'::jsonb, 'Soonr’s focus on both partners matches clinical advice: ACOG’s prepregnancy guidance covers diet and a prenatal vitamin with folic acid, exercise, a healthy weight, and cutting out tobacco and alcohol, and partners’ habits matter too. An app that makes those habits shared and visible may help couples stay consistent, though no study of Soonr itself was found.

For timing, fertile-window predictions based on period logs are estimates. Urine LH testing is better supported: a 2023 Cochrane review found timing sex with ovulation tests probably improves pregnancy and live-birth rates, which is why pairing the app with a test reader can help. ACOG recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying, or 6 months if you’re over 35.', 'On the App Store, Soonr has a 4.7-star average from 21 ratings (as of September 30, 2026), a small number since the app launched in February 2026. Read the reviews directly on the App Store and Google Play listings linked below.', 'No independent study of the Soonr app was found. Its fertile-window predictions are estimates; urine ovulation testing, which it can log and sync, has moderate-quality Cochrane evidence for improving pregnancy rates.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance and a Cochrane review; not a direct clinician quote. App details are from soonr.health, its App Store listing, and its privacy policy.', 'curated', false, false, 4.7, true, '{"userRatingSourceUrl":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","platform":"iOS, Android","website":"https://soonr.health/","whereToBuyLinks":{"App Store":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","Google Play":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.health.soonr"},"privacy":{"dataStorage":"AWS servers in the United States and other countries, per Soonr’s privacy policy. Operated by Vespexx Inc.","sellsData":"Says it does not sell personal data or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.","hipaa":"Not described as HIPAA-covered; consumer wellness app.","keyPolicy":"Health data is shared with a connected partner only with your explicit consent, and disconnecting removes previously shared data from the partner’s app."},"doctorOpinionShort":"A couples’ preconception tracker built around ACOG-style healthy habits for both partners. Fertile-window predictions are estimates; pairing it with LH testing, which Cochrane evidence supports, is more precise. No study of the app itself was found.","whoItsFor":["Couples planning a pregnancy who want to work on health habits together","Partners who want to see each other’s cycle calendar, fertile window, and daily logs","Anyone who wants to log ovulation tests and BBT alongside lifestyle habits"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Soonr’s own getting-started steps:","steps":["Download the app and answer a few questions about your health, lifestyle, and goals.","Invite your partner with a link; you both agree on what health data is shared.","Log daily health factors (exercise, meals, symptoms, supplements, habits) in about 5 minutes a day.","Track your cycle; Soonr predicts the fertile window and shows it on a shared calendar.","Optional: connect the Surearly SMART reader (sold separately) for LH and progesterone-marker readings."],"sourceUrl":"https://soonr.health/","sourceLabel":"soonr.health"},"warnings":["Soonr is a wellness tool, not medical advice or a diagnosis.","Not a form of birth control.","See a clinician if you haven’t conceived after 1 year of trying (6 months if you’re over 35), per ACOG."],"integrations":["Apple Health","Surearly SMART"],"badges":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10501857/","text":"Timed intercourse for couples trying to conceive (Cochrane review, 2023)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 7 randomized trials (2,464 women or couples) found that timing sex with urine ovulation (LH) tests probably increases the chance of pregnancy and live birth compared with not predicting ovulation (moderate-quality evidence). This supports ovulation testing in general, not a specific device or app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/good-health-before-pregnancy-prepregnancy-care","text":"ACOG: Good Health Before Pregnancy (Prepregnancy Care)","summary":"ACOG recommends steps before pregnancy such as a healthy diet and prenatal vitamin with folic acid, regular exercise, reaching a healthy weight, and stopping tobacco, alcohol, and other substances, and notes partners shouldn’t smoke around you. These are the kinds of habits the Soonr app tracks; this is general guidance, not validation of the app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/evaluating-infertility","text":"ACOG: Evaluating Infertility","summary":"ACOG explains that urine tests detect the rise in luteinizing hormone (LH) that comes before ovulation, and recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying (or 6 months if you’re over 35). This is clinical guidance for the category, not validation of a specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","text":"App Store: Soonr: Fertility for Couples","summary":"The app’s App Store listing: 4.7 stars from 21 ratings as of September 30, 2026."},{"url":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.health.soonr","text":"Google Play: Soonr","summary":"The app’s Google Play listing, with Android user reviews."},{"url":"https://soonr.health/","text":"soonr.health","summary":"Soonr’s own site, with features and pricing."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-surearly-smart-ovulation-test', 'Surearly SMART Ovulation Test Reader (works with Soonr)', 'Surearly', 'diagnostics', 'physical', 'A digital at-home urine test reader that measures two hormones from one stick: LH, whose surge predicts your fertile window, and P3G (a progesterone marker, also called PdG), which confirms ovulation happened. Results appear on the reader in about 5 minutes and sync by Bluetooth to the Soonr app (or Surearly’s own app), where you can see hormone trends across cycles and share them with a partner. Comes with 20 test sticks. Made by Sugentech (Surearly); Soonr sells it as its recommended hormone tester.', 'See Amazon for current price (reader + 20 test sticks)', '/products/soonr/surearly-smart-reader.webp', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1BCL6NB?tag=aynahealth-20', '["fertility","pregnancy"]'::jsonb, '["fertility","cycle-tracking"]'::jsonb, '["Amazon"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Listed in the FDA’s device database (GUDID) as an over-the-counter LH test (product code NGE) made by Sugentech; no 510(k) clearance is listed. Soonr also describes it as CE-IVD marked.","materials":"Digital test reader with Bluetooth, plus 20 single-use urine test sticks. Detects LH at 10 mIU/mL or above and progesterone metabolite (P3G) at 5 µg/mL or above, per its FDA device listing.","recalls":"No recalls are listed in its FDA device record; check current FDA and manufacturer notices.","sideEffects":"None expected (urine test). Full notes are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"Accuracy figures (the box claims over 99% accuracy at detecting the LH surge) are the manufacturer’s. Surearly and Soonr are separate companies; Soonr promotes the device and its app syncs with it."}'::jsonb, 'Urine LH testing is one of the better-supported tools for trying to conceive: ACOG explains that these tests detect the LH rise before ovulation, and a 2023 Cochrane review found timing sex with ovulation tests probably increases pregnancy and live-birth rates (moderate-quality evidence). Adding a progesterone-marker (P3G/PdG) reading can help confirm that ovulation actually happened, which LH alone can’t show.

The reader’s digital result removes the guesswork of reading faint lines. No independent study of this specific reader was found, and ovulation tests can’t diagnose infertility; ACOG recommends an evaluation after 1 year of trying, or 6 months if you’re over 35.', 'Customer reviews for this reader are on its Amazon listing (linked below). Amazon blocks automated access, so ayna hasn’t pulled a rating; read them directly.', 'Urine LH testing probably improves pregnancy and live-birth rates when used to time sex (Cochrane 2023, moderate-quality evidence). No independent study of the Surearly SMART reader was found.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance, a Cochrane review, and the device’s FDA listing; not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"LH ovulation testing has moderate-quality Cochrane evidence for improving pregnancy rates, and adding a progesterone-marker reading helps confirm ovulation. No study of this specific reader was found.","whoItsFor":["People trying to conceive who want to pinpoint their fertile window","Anyone who wants to confirm ovulation happened, not just predict it","Soonr app users who want real hormone readings synced to their shared calendar"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Soonr and the device’s FDA listing:","steps":["Insert a test stick into the reader and apply urine as directed on the package insert.","Read the result on the reader in about 5 minutes.","Results sync by Bluetooth to the Soonr app (or the Surearly SMART app), where you can track LH and P3G across cycles."],"sourceUrl":"https://soonr.health/","sourceLabel":"soonr.health: Surearly SMART"},"warnings":["Follow the package insert for when in your cycle to start testing and what time of day to test.","Ovulation tests predict and confirm ovulation; they can’t diagnose infertility or confirm pregnancy.","See a clinician if you haven’t conceived after 1 year of trying (6 months if you’re over 35), per ACOG."],"integrations":["Soonr","Surearly SMART app"],"badges":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10501857/","text":"Timed intercourse for couples trying to conceive (Cochrane review, 2023)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 7 randomized trials (2,464 women or couples) found that timing sex with urine ovulation (LH) tests probably increases the chance of pregnancy and live birth compared with not predicting ovulation (moderate-quality evidence). This supports ovulation testing in general, not a specific device or app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/evaluating-infertility","text":"ACOG: Evaluating Infertility","summary":"ACOG explains that urine tests detect the rise in luteinizing hormone (LH) that comes before ovulation, and recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying (or 6 months if you’re over 35). This is clinical guidance for the category, not validation of a specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"amazon","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1BCL6NB","text":"Amazon: Surearly Digital Fertility Monitor, LH + PdG Ovulation Tracker with App","summary":"This reader’s Amazon listing (reader + 20 test sticks), with customer reviews. Amazon blocks automated access, so no rating is quoted here; read the reviews directly."},{"url":"https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/devices/08809408863482","text":"FDA device listing (GUDID): Surearly SMART Ovulation Test","summary":"The device’s entry in the FDA/NIH device database: over-the-counter LH test by Sugentech, in commercial distribution."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb)
